=== PARITY (vs web ActionBuilder.tsx) ===
  Web source is a controlled form: props { actions, channels, onChange }; it renders an
  ordered list of action editor cards over a GlassPanel and an "Add Action" button. Each
  card has a numbered index, an Action Type select (label only on row 0), the kind-specific
  fields, and move-up/move-down/remove controls.

  Data sources -> useTranslation only (no data hook). The native model binds the actions +
    channels the host supplies and pushes a fresh [AutomationAction] on every edit via
    onChange (web `onChange`). The view performs NO networking — structurally enforced (the
    view only reads ActionBuilderModel; the model only emits onChange).
  Action kinds (all 4) ->
    action_command: command select (web commandOptions: "Select command..." sentinel + every
      group's commands as "${group} - ${command}") + Params(JSON, optional) editor. The params
      editor reproduces the web local state + validation effect exactly: empty clears params,
      a JSON OBJECT commits, a non-object shows "Params must be a JSON object." and a malformed
      string shows "Invalid JSON" — neither commits. Seeding = JSON.stringify(params, null, 2)
      (order-preserving), so a valid edit reformats to pretty just like the web useEffect.
    action_notify: channel select (disabled channels are unselectable like the web `disabled`
      option; "No channels configured" sentinel when channels is empty) + Message editor.
    action_set_setting: Setting Key input + Value Type select (text/number/boolean) + the value
      editor that flips between a True/False select and a text/number input. Coercions ported
      verbatim: number = parseFloat(v)||0, boolean = v=="true", display via String(Number).
    action_call_automation: Target Automation ID number input — shows empty for the 0 sentinel,
      coerces via parseInt(v)||0.
  Catalog -> ACTION_TYPES (4) + COMMAND_GROUPS (7 groups / 29 commands) ported entry-for-entry.
  defaultChannelId -> first enabled channel ?? first channel ?? 0 (web memo).
  Row mechanics -> numbered "N.", move-up disabled on first / move-down disabled on last, remove;
    Add Action appends a default command action seeded with the default channel id.
  Shared components -> web @/components/ui {Input, Select, Button, GlassPanel, Textarea} map to the
    REAL apps/apple TSButton + .tsGlassPanel() material and token-driven native field/select rows
    (the FleetVehiclePicker idiom: a menu Picker with verbatim option labels + token chrome). All
    chrome compiled against the real Tokens/TSMaterial/Buttons in the typechecks below. Recharts ->
    none / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> empty (friendly inline hint, never a blank box) · content (the action
    cards) · per-field sub-states: JSON object-error, JSON malformed-error, "No channels configured",
    and the text/number/boolean value editors. loading/error/stale/offline are N/A for a controlled
    form with no async data of its own (same disposition as 0040 RequestBuilder).
  i18n -> every web key resolves through the P1/S10 facade; 0 English literals in native code (all
    via ActionBuilderStrings). The 5 "...Placeholder" web keys are isolated behind parity:allow.
  a11y -> every interactive control (type/command/channel/value-type/value selects, key/message/
    params/target fields, move/remove/add buttons) carries an accessibilityLabel; each card is an
    accessibilityElement(.contain) labelled "Action N"; the params error is static-text. Row label
    content is unit-tested via ActionBuilderAccessibility.
  Telemetry -> ActionBuilderModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"ActionBuilder") once (P1/S11).
    Asserted by a spy in the executed suite.

